<BaseLayout title="About — Raashid Arquil" description="Independent developer building my own products, and websites and apps for others."><div class="shell">
<header class="page-intro compact-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1 class="display">The person<br/><em class="serif">behind the work.</em></h1></header>
<section class="about-grid revised-about"><aside><div class="portrait-frame"><OptimizedImage src="/images/profile.jpg" alt="Raashid Arquil" width="360" height="450" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 110px, 310px" loading="eager"/></div><p class="identity-name">Raashid Arquil</p><p class="small-copy">Independent developer · From problem to product</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt class="eyebrow">Education</dt><dd>B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science<br/>First Class · Kingston University</dd></div><div><dt class="eyebrow">Also studied</dt><dd>PG Diploma, Professional Marketing<br/>CIM Level 7 · Merit<br/>Distinctions in two modules</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link mt-6" href="/resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a></aside>
<div class="article-body"><p>I build websites and mobile applications, and I'm developing my own products alongside continuing study.</p><p>I care that the software has a purpose. Before deciding what to build, I want to understand what someone is trying to do, what is difficult, and whether software can help.</p><p>Sometimes the starting point is personal. KeepClose came from forgetting people I don't meet often. SmartDrive came from the calls, books, and queues I dealt with while getting my driving licence.</p><h2>How I work</h2><p>I define the scope and user flows, research technical choices, and refine the implementation. I use AI throughout development, including implementation. It helps me move quickly; understanding the result and its limitations remains part of the work.</p><p>I'm currently building KeepClose, CropCare, and Tally.</p></div>
</section><ContactBanner/>
</div></BaseLayout>
